From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] J604 local build: blur the Glassy bar from the cached
 backdrop (xray)

The omarchy-bar layer covers the whole screen (1512x982 on the J604), so
with the Glassy bar on, Hyprland re-blurs the live content behind the full
layer on every damaged frame. On the J604 that costs about 7.6 ms of GPU
time per frame and holds a 120 Hz panel at 59 fps.

With xray set on the bar's own layer rule, Hyprland blurs the bar from the
cached blur of the wallpaper layer instead of from the live windows behind
it. The bar stays frosted; windows passing behind it are no longer seen
blurred through it. Global blur (windows, popups) is unchanged.

MEASURED on the J604: the same
layer rule plus xray = true gave 119 fps at 120 Hz with GPU in-fences p50
2.9 ms (was 59 fps, 7.8 ms); a global decoration:blur:xray = true did not
(59 fps).

Only the toggle source in /usr/share/omarchy changes. An existing
~/.local/state/omarchy/toggles/hypr/bar-glassy.lua is a copy that
omarchy-bar sync_glass() writes only when it is missing, so it takes this
change when the bar background is set to glassy again.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>

---
 default/hypr/toggles/bar-glassy.lua | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/default/hypr/toggles/bar-glassy.lua b/default/hypr/toggles/bar-glassy.lua
index a7ed7e0a37..212ddc0c75 100644
--- a/default/hypr/toggles/bar-glassy.lua
+++ b/default/hypr/toggles/bar-glassy.lua
@@ -6,4 +6,5 @@ hl.layer_rule({
   match = { namespace = "^omarchy-bar$" },
   blur = true,
   ignore_alpha = 0.3,
+  xray = true,
 })
